From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] PC5: memory a game asks to share is ordinary memory
 when the console can't share it (Wine patch 0937)

DXVK making a shared texture for an Unreal Engine 5 game on Direct3D
12 (STRETCHER.MEN) asked Wine for memory it could share as a Win32
handle. Wine exports that through the host's VK_KHR_external_memory_fd,
which the PS5's RADV lacks: the allocation failed ("Unsupported handle
type 0") and the game crashed calling a null function. The memory is now
an ordinary allocation, as on a driver that shares nothing.
