 | 0934 | `nsi`: without `\\.\Nsi` (a PS5 title starts no `winedevice.exe`, so no `nsiproxy.sys`) the NSI requests are answered in `nsi.dll` with the software loopback interface alone, as Windows always has it: the NDIS interface table and index-to-LUID map, and the IPv4 and IPv6 interface and unicast tables (127.0.0.1/8, ::1/128), filled as `nsiproxy.sys` fills a Unix `lo`; the other tables list no rows. `GetAdaptersAddresses`, `GetIfTable`, `GetIpAddrTable` and the like failed with error 2, and Java's `NetworkInterface` threw an Error on that: Shattered Pixel Dungeon closed when it started a new game. With the device nothing changes |
 | 0935 | `ntdll`: when the kernel doesn't apply a 0928 repair (the same fault again within a millisecond, in the same state), the faulting instruction, a plain MOV of a byte or a dword between a register and a `%fs:` operand, is done by the handler on the 32-bit TEB and the thread goes on after it; the thread's later faulting `%fs:` MOVs are done so at once, with the repair still written into each frame. falloutwHR.exe was repaired once in `GetStdHandle`, then faulted 64 times in a row in `RtlEnterCriticalSection` (`mov %fs:0x18,%eax`) and crashed. The first miss is logged with the frame's selector and base |
 | 0936 | `ntdll`: a directory whose handle the server keeps no Unix name for (patch 0140 enters directories by that name) is entered by the Unix name of its NT name (`\??\C:\...`), as `NtCreateFile` resolves it; `NtQueryDirectoryFile` failed with `STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE` (`fchdir`'s `EBADF`), and .NET's `FileSystemEnumerator` threw "invalid handle" for a game's folder (Heroes of Might and Magic: Olden Era, `StreamingAssets\maps\Story_maps`), whose maps then never loaded. A directory still not entered is logged with which name failed and why |
+| 0937 | `win32u`: memory a program asks `vkAllocateMemory` for as shareable (`VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo` with Win32 handle types) is an ordinary allocation when the host can't export memory: the PS5's RADV has no `VK_KHR_external_memory_fd`, so the export failed ("Unsupported handle type 0") and the allocation with it. DXVK making a shared texture for an Unreal Engine 5 game on Direct3D 12 (STRETCHER.MEN) got no memory, and the game crashed calling a null function; now it gets its memory, and a handle for it can't be had |
 | 0972 | `faudio` (Wine's bundled FAudio 26.09): upstream FAudio a3b49d6 and 2ead980 (2026-09-26). A source voice that played at the output rate never advanced `resampleOffset`, so when it started resampling, the tap loops of `FAudio_INTERNAL_MixSource` ran from the stale offset, `toResample - tap_samples` wrapped and the SSE2 resampler wrote far past `resampled_audio`. A game corrupted its process heap and crashed in the mixer, or in the heap. FAudio is a static library, so every `xaudio2_*` and `xactengine*` module is in `PE_MODULES` |
 
